"""Native, shared two-member Bundle pavement and automatic separator surface.

The fixed-axis mapping uses actual physical offset boundaries and proves that
each has a monotone projection and matching terminal cuts. It supports curved
members without assuming that equal control rank pairs valid cross-sections.
Every boundary knot and interval-order event is a mandatory row. Positive cell
Jacobians and the complete outer perimeter are checked as well; the independent
continuous centerline-contact guard belongs to the caller.

Three direct Grid bands cover the corridor exactly once.  The central mesh band
has a positive width even in overlaps, but the *profile* plateau is strictly
max(signed inner-edge gap, 0).  Keeping these two widths separate avoids zero
area faces at the disappearance of a separator.  On mixed spans, a finite-width
rounded material cap ends each grass island before the geometric pinch point.
All construction and classifications are Geometry Nodes fields: no evaluated
mesh, island partition or current source position is supplied by Python.
"""

